00:00:26.223 --> 00:00:27.511
I feel like I'm in the flow of things.

00:00:27.511 --> 00:00:28.975
It's all good. It's great. Thank you.

00:00:28.975 --> 00:00:29.841
- [Kelly] Oh, I love that.

00:00:29.841 --> 00:00:30.674
- Thank you.

00:00:30.674 --> 00:00:33.507
- I also hear that you're
now of a very exclusive club.

00:00:33.507 --> 00:00:34.374
I wanna get this right.

00:00:34.374 --> 00:00:36.003
It's in Hollywood, it's called TCT

00:00:36.003 --> 00:00:36.839
- [Raymond] That's right.

00:00:36.839 --> 00:00:37.916
- T C C C.

00:00:37.916 --> 00:00:38.749
- Um-hmm.

00:00:38.749 --> 00:00:40.765
- [Kelly] What is that? What is that?

00:00:40.765 --> 00:00:41.879
How do I get in?

00:00:41.879 --> 00:00:43.967
- The first two letters are Tom Cruise.

00:00:43.967 --> 00:00:44.800
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.279
- And the other letters are coconut cake.

00:00:48.279 --> 00:00:49.435
- [Kelly] Coconut cake.

00:00:49.435 --> 00:00:50.687
- Is it coconut or Christmas?

00:00:50.687 --> 00:00:51.520
- [Angela] I think it's Christmas cake

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:52.353
- Is it a Christmas cake?

00:00:52.353 --> 00:00:53.186
- Oh, Christmas cake?

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:54.019
- TCCC.

00:00:54.019 --> 00:00:54.852
(all laughing)

00:00:54.852 --> 00:00:55.685
- Wait, wait.

00:00:55.685 --> 00:00:56.518
Did you get a cake too?

00:00:56.518 --> 00:00:57.351
- [Angela] I get a cake.

00:00:57.351 --> 00:00:58.184
- You've got a cake.

00:00:58.184 --> 00:00:59.017
- [Angela] I get a cake.

00:00:59.017 --> 00:01:00.145
- [Raymond] I get a cake, you get a cake.

00:01:00.145 --> 00:01:03.591
- I didn't get a cake.
I like cake, Tom Cruise.

00:01:03.591 --> 00:01:04.539
(everyone laughing)

00:01:04.539 --> 00:01:05.533
I like cake.

00:01:05.533 --> 00:01:06.706
Is it the most delicious cake ever?

00:01:06.706 --> 00:01:07.704
- [Raymond] It's the most delicious cake.

00:01:07.704 --> 00:01:10.156
It's up to the standard
of Tom Cruise standards.

00:01:10.156 --> 00:01:11.386
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:01:11.386 --> 00:01:12.239
- It's a coconut cake.

00:01:12.239 --> 00:01:13.072
- My mouth is watering.

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:13.905
- It's so good.

00:01:13.905 --> 00:01:16.595
I've had it dipped in resin
and I've had it preserved

00:01:16.595 --> 00:01:18.627
on my house, cause one day I'll eat it,

00:01:18.627 --> 00:01:20.499
but yeah, I've heard it's great.

00:01:20.499 --> 00:01:21.640
No, it's so amazing.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:24.999
- It's so good that at
our 25th anniversary,

00:01:24.999 --> 00:01:25.832
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:25.832 --> 00:01:26.665
- We had the cake.

00:01:26.665 --> 00:01:29.582
We had a three tiered TCC-CCC cake.

00:01:31.006 --> 00:01:31.839
(all laughing)

00:01:31.839 --> 00:01:32.696
- Oh wow.

00:01:32.696 --> 00:01:34.523
- [Angela] And I ate the
second tier all by myself.

00:01:34.523 --> 00:01:35.579
- [Kelly] What's this cake?

00:01:35.579 --> 00:01:36.412
(all laughing)

00:01:36.412 --> 00:01:38.090
- Was it delivered to you in the same way

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:38.982
it was delivered to me

00:01:38.982 --> 00:01:41.517
because on Christmas Eve there
was just a knock on my door

00:01:41.517 --> 00:01:43.411
and I was really close to the door,

00:01:43.411 --> 00:01:45.415
so I was only maybe about
three seconds away from it,

00:01:45.415 --> 00:01:47.214
I opened, there was no one there.

00:01:47.214 --> 00:01:49.213
And then I looked down and
there was just a pink box.

00:01:49.213 --> 00:01:50.046
- [Kelly] Hoo.

00:01:50.046 --> 00:01:50.898
- [Raymond] And it says-

00:01:50.898 --> 00:01:51.731
- [Angela] Yep. That's it.

00:01:51.731 --> 00:01:52.564
- [Raymond] It says warmest wishes to you

00:01:52.564 --> 00:01:53.946
this holiday season, Tom Cruise.

00:01:53.946 --> 00:01:54.779
- [Kelly] What?

00:01:54.779 --> 00:01:55.612
- [Raymond] Yeah.

00:01:55.612 --> 00:01:56.445
(audience clapping)

00:01:56.445 --> 00:01:58.325
And it was like, it was
as if he dropped by like,

00:01:58.325 --> 00:02:01.194
on a jet pack and just flew away.

00:02:01.194 --> 00:02:02.702
- You know what, it's
Tom Cruise, maybe he did.

00:02:02.702 --> 00:02:03.888
- Yeah, I mean, I, believe it.

00:02:03.888 --> 00:02:04.902
- I feel like he'd try it.

00:02:04.902 --> 00:02:05.735
(both guests laughing)

00:02:05.735 --> 00:02:07.375
I feel like he'd be like,
I'll try, let's do it. Yeah.

00:02:07.375 --> 00:02:08.208
(Raymond laughing)

00:02:08.208 --> 00:02:09.041
I feel like he's that guy, right?

00:02:09.041 --> 00:02:09.874
Mission impossible.

00:02:09.874 --> 00:02:10.707
- [Raymond] That's right.

00:02:10.707 --> 00:02:11.540
- He can try any of those things.

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:12.373
- [Raymond] That's right.

00:02:12.373 --> 00:02:13.206
- I actually wanna try a
jet pack and eat the cake.

00:02:13.206 --> 00:02:14.110
Whatever, Tom.

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:15.943
(guest laughing)

00:02:15.943 --> 00:02:17.113
So you were here before talking about,

00:02:17.113 --> 00:02:19.598
it was before Quantum Leap premiered,

00:02:19.598 --> 00:02:23.127
so did you know, did you
think it would be a success?

00:02:23.127 --> 00:02:25.834
- You know, it's hard to know
if anything you're working

00:02:25.834 --> 00:02:27.360
on is gonna be great.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:29.662
You read the scripts and you
go, "Okay, this is great."

00:02:29.662 --> 00:02:31.155
And then you do the days and you go,

00:02:31.155 --> 00:02:31.988
"Okay, that was a great scene."

00:02:31.988 --> 00:02:32.821
And then you just take it a scene

00:02:32.821 --> 00:02:34.291
at a time and it feels good.

00:02:34.291 --> 00:02:36.071
The ensemble's good, the scripts are good,

00:02:36.071 --> 00:02:37.098
the producers are good.

00:02:37.098 --> 00:02:38.194
Everyone's saying it's great.

00:02:38.194 --> 00:02:40.782
And then it goes up and then
you hope people watch it

00:02:40.782 --> 00:02:41.627
and then people watch it

00:02:41.627 --> 00:02:44.202
and then you realize it's
something that people

00:02:44.202 --> 00:02:47.822
are gravitating towards and
you go, "Oh, thank God."

00:02:47.822 --> 00:02:48.823
You know, what a relief.

00:02:48.823 --> 00:02:49.946
- Well, I think it's so interesting

00:02:49.946 --> 00:02:52.451
cause y'all put a lot in other
people's hands as actors.

00:02:52.451 --> 00:02:54.079
Cause like, as a musician,

00:02:54.079 --> 00:02:55.654
I'm there for the whole
process of this song.

00:02:55.654 --> 00:02:58.523
Like, you see every version of
it right, before it goes out.

00:02:58.523 --> 00:03:00.283
But as actors, like,

00:03:00.283 --> 00:03:02.000
sometimes you only see
the clips that you're in.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.486
You don't see it all together.

00:03:03.486 --> 00:03:05.434
So then, it's hard to know, probably.

00:03:05.434 --> 00:03:06.499
- It's impossible to know.

00:03:06.499 --> 00:03:07.332
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:07.332 --> 00:03:08.165
- You go in and you do,

00:03:08.165 --> 00:03:09.084
- It's a lot of trust tree going on there.

00:03:09.084 --> 00:03:10.547
- Absolutely. It takes a village.

00:03:10.547 --> 00:03:12.383
And we wouldn't be able to do anything

00:03:12.383 --> 00:03:14.287
without our crew, our incredible crew.

00:03:14.287 --> 00:03:15.806
So, they're working harder than I am.

00:03:15.806 --> 00:03:16.639
- [Kelly] Oh man, yeah.

00:03:16.639 --> 00:03:17.643
- So yeah, it's incredible.

00:03:17.643 --> 00:03:19.609
- [Kelly] I think every crew
on every show works harder

00:03:19.609 --> 00:03:20.655
than everybody else.

00:03:20.655 --> 00:03:21.621
Their always the first ones there,

00:03:21.621 --> 00:03:22.535
the last ones to breakdown.

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:23.486
- That's right. That's right.

00:03:23.486 --> 00:03:24.759
- [Kelly] Same thing in
the musician world, yeah.

00:03:24.759 --> 00:03:28.266
- Well, the fall finale of
Quantum Leap airs tonight

00:03:28.266 --> 00:03:31.050
at 10 on NBC and be sure to catch

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:33.103
up on the entire season
streaming on Peacock.

